{"id":997,"date":"2020-11-17T11:52:14","date_gmt":"2020-11-17T19:52:14","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=997"},"modified":"2024-09-01T20:17:43","modified_gmt":"2024-09-02T03:17:43","slug":"codrone-arduino-variables","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-variables\/","title":{"rendered":"Variables"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215c332869\" name=\"6a2215c332869\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are variables?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Variables are important in all programming languages and in most programs! Just like in math, variables in programming are placeholders and data storage for numbers. Typically, you can create a variable and save its value at the beginning of your program, and then you can recall that value later on in the program whenever you use the variable.<\/p>\n<p>Let&#8217;s go through an example! Sometimes the baud rate for your CoDrone can be hard to remember &#8212; is it 112500 or 115200? (It&#8217;s 115200) Instead of racking your brain, you can save the baud rate&#8217;s value as a variable, which would look like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int x = 115200;<\/pre>\n<p>Now, 115200 is stored in the variable x! Every time you use x in your program, you can imagine that it&#8217;s replaced by 115200.<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint x = 115200;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    CoDrone.begin(x);     \/\/same as CoDrone.begin(115200)\r\n    CoDrone.pair();\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop () {\r\n}<\/pre>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215c332a04\" name=\"6a2215c332a04\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Using variables<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]There are three steps to using a variable:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Initialization &#8211; creates the variable in your program<\/li>\n<li>Storage &#8211; stores the value of your variable<\/li>\n<li>Call &#8211; uses your variable&#8217;s value later in your program<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Initializing your variable<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Before you use a variable, you have to initialize it.\u00a0Initialization\u00a0always follows this format:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">DataType VariableName<\/pre>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>For example, <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">int Example<\/code>would initialize an integer variable named Example.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215c332a90\" name=\"6a2215c332a90\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Data types<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>You might have been confused by data types in the last step! Data types are important because they determine how much data each variable can store. Make sure you pick the right one for your program!<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">byte<\/code>&#8211; A byte. Can be any whole number from 0 to 255<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">int<\/code>&#8211; An integer. Can be any whole number from -32,768 to 32,767<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">long<\/code>&#8211; A long. Can be any whole number from -2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__question\">\n<div class=\"styled-checkbox activity2__button-checkbox\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215c332b01\" name=\"6a2215c332b01\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Variable names<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can name your variable whatever you want, as long as there are no spaces or special characters. One example is <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">int HappyFace123<\/code>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Declaring a value<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>When you declare a variable, its value is automatically 0. If you don&#8217;t want your variable&#8217;s value to be equal to 0, you can set an initial value. For example, if you wanted to change <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">HappyFace123<\/code>&#8216;s value to equal 10, you would need to write:<\/p>\n<div class=\"CodeMirror notranslate cm-s-default\">\n<div>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int HappyFace123 = 10<\/pre>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215c332b9e\" name=\"6a2215c332b9e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Scope<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The scope of a variable is a very important thing to keep in mind when you&#8217;re programming. The scope determines where in your program your variable exists. If you try to use a variable outside of its scope, the compiler will show an error saying\u00a0&#8220;not declared in this scope&#8221;.<\/p>\n<p>General rule for scope: a variable can only be used within the brackets it&#8217;s initialized in.<\/p>\n<p>Here are a few examples:<\/p>\n<p><strong>Example 1<\/strong><\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void setup(){ \/\/BRACKET START\r\n\/\/x is initialzed inside the setup's brackets\r\nint x; \r\nx=2;\r\n}             \/\/BRACKET END\r\n\r\nvoid loop(){\r\nx=1; \/\/running this will give an error\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>x\u00a0 is initialized within the brackets of <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code>, so it can only be used within these brackets. x = 2\u00a0 works fine since it is within <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code> as well. However, when you try to set x = 1 in <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void loop()<\/code>, you&#8217;ll get a scope error because it is not within the same set of brackets.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Example 2<\/strong><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void setup(){ \r\n\r\nif(true){\/\/BRACKET START\r\n    int x; \r\n    x=1;\r\n    }\/\/BRACKET END\r\n\r\nx=2; \/\/running this will give an error\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>x\u00a0 is initialized within the brackets of <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">if(true)<\/code>, so it can only be used within these brackets. x=1 works fine, since it is within <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">if(true)<\/code> brackets. When you try to set x=2 in <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code> outside of the if statement, you&#8217;ll get a scope error because it is not within the same set of brackets.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Example 3<\/strong><\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int x;\r\n\r\nvoid setup(){     \r\n    x=1;\r\n}             \r\n\r\nvoid loop(){\r\n    x=2;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>This example works! The variable x is initialized before <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code> and outside of any brackets. This is called a global variable and can be used anywhere in the program.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215c332c24\" name=\"6a2215c332c24\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Variable math<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Variables in programming can be changed really easily using mathematical operations. Your math teacher will be so excited to hear this!<\/p>\n<p><strong>Mathematical Operations<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Addition:\u00a0<code class=\"code-snippet-inline\">x=y+z\u00a0<\/code><\/p>\n<p>Subtraction:\u00a0<code class=\"code-snippet-inline\">x=y-z\u00a0<\/code><\/p>\n<p>Multiplication:\u00a0<code class=\"code-snippet-inline\">x=y*z\u00a0<\/code><\/p>\n<p>Division:\u00a0<code class=\"code-snippet-inline\">x=y\/z<\/code><\/p>\n<p><strong>Example 1<\/strong><\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int y = 4;\r\nint z = 3;\r\nint x = y + z;<\/pre>\n<p>After adding the values of y and z, x = 7.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Example 2<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>That equals sign you see doesn&#8217;t mean &#8220;equals&#8221; or &#8220;is equal to&#8221;. In programming, it means &#8220;gets the value of&#8221;, which should help you understand what we&#8217;re about to tell you.<\/p>\n<p>One of the things you can do in programming is change a variable&#8217;s value in its own equation. For example:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int y = 4;\r\nint x = 3;\r\nx = y + x;<\/pre>\n<p>The old value of x\u00a0was 3, but then it was used in the equation x = 4 + 3.\u00a0The new value of x\u00a0is now 7.<\/p>\n<p>We know this seems weird and confusing, but we promise that it&#8217;s normal.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215c332c9e\" name=\"6a2215c332c9e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Challenge:\u00a0Variable square<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Use the setup code provided to have your CoDrone take off and then fly in a square pattern!<\/p>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>You are only allowed to use the existing variables, but you can change the values.<\/li>\n<li>You can&#8217;t use any numbers after you initialize the variables! The only exception is the baud rate.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Setup code<\/strong><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint A = 1;\r\nint B = 500;\r\nint C = 5;\r\nint D = 2;\r\nint E = 10;\r\nint F = 3;\r\n\r\nvoid setup(){  \r\n    CoDrone.begin(115200);  \r\n    CoDrone.pair();\r\n\r\n    CoDrone.takeoff();   \r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop(){\r\n    byte bt8 = digitalRead(18);\r\n    byte bt4 = digitalRead(14);\r\n    byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n\r\n    if(bt1 &amp;&amp; bt4 &amp;&amp; !bt8){\r\n        CoDrone.emergencyStop();\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p><strong>Example code<\/strong><\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint A = 1;\r\nint B = 500;\r\nint C = 5;\r\nint D = 2;\r\nint E = 10;\r\nint F = 3;\r\n\r\nvoid setup(){  \r\n    CoDrone.begin(115200);  \r\n    CoDrone.pair();  \r\n\r\n    CoDrone.takeoff();  \r\n    CoDrone.move(D);  \r\n\r\n    CoDrone.setThrottle((C * C) * F);  \/\/5 * 5 * 3  = 75; move at 75% power throttle for 2 seconds\r\n    CoDrone.move(A * D);             \/\/ 1 * 2 = 2  \r\n\r\n    CoDrone.setThrottle(0);          \/\/ Zero out the throttle\r\n    CoDrone.move(); \r\n\r\n    CoDrone.land();                    \r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop(){\r\n    byte bt8 = digitalRead(18);\r\n    byte bt4 = digitalRead(14);\r\n    byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n\r\n    if(bt1 &amp;&amp; bt4 &amp;&amp; !bt8){\r\n        CoDrone.emergencyStop();\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 What are variables? [vc_column_text]Variables are important in all programming languages and in most programs! Just like in math, variables in programming are placeholders and data storage for&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-variables\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1751,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1737,1782,1848,1793,1826,1482,853,694,1392,282,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2135,2164,2165,2123,2122,2117],"class_list":["post-997","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-variables","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/997","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/997\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1001,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/997\/revisions\/1001"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1751"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=997"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=997"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=997"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}